				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-359137#post-4738017</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-359137/scp-620#post-4738017</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2020 04:16:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>KleptocracyNow</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4875396</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This reminds me of time magic in Pact (a webserial, it's unrelated to SCP). While it's technically possible to use magic to affect time itself, it's incredibly costly, with people using hours of days of their life just to be able to tweak a second or two.</p> <p>So what chronomancers usually do is use magic to affects people's perception of time, much like this scip. And I like both. Altering perception is a powerful thing.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
